{"id":"1266410053654855680","date":"2020-05-29","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1266410053654855680","author":"adamdangelo","text":"Open sourcing our internal python static analysis tool.  https://t.co/ZKnV00XGlP","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200529215448","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200529215448/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1266410053654855680","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1265476562289258499","date":"2020-05-27","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476562289258499","author":"adamdangelo","text":"This may sound too optimistic but you need to remember that in-person meetings are usually far from optimal. It takes a lot of work and skill to run a meeting well, and offloading this to the software could take a lot of burden off the moderator and greatly improve most meetings.","reply_to":"adamdangelo","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200527195753","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200527195753/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476562289258499","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1265476561622319105","date":"2020-05-27","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476561622319105","author":"adamdangelo","text":"With enough of these, and some other improvements (like head tracking to stay appropriately zoomed in like FB Portal), I believe we can eventually get to the point where group meetings are more efficient over Zoom than they are in person.","reply_to":"adamdangelo","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200527154308","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200527154308/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476561622319105","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1265476560947048450","date":"2020-05-27","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476560947048450","author":"adamdangelo","text":"We need company-appropriate sounds, graphics, and animations, rules for who gets prompted when and what each person can do, and varying levels of prominence and structure that can be crafted appropriately for the situation.","reply_to":"adamdangelo","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200527062537","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200527062537/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476560947048450","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1265476560250736640","date":"2020-05-27","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476560250736640","author":"adamdangelo","text":"The Zoom chat and the simple thumbs up signals aren't good enough. They're not integrated into the actual video and they shouldn't be. Different meetings and different cultures require different interactions, hence the need for a flexible platform.","reply_to":"adamdangelo","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200527065848","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200527065848/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476560250736640","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1265476559479046144","date":"2020-05-27","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476559479046144","author":"adamdangelo","text":"Or a \"brainstorm mode\" could only support +1's that are directed at specific people and disappear after a few seconds. Or an \"N minutes until meeting is over\" reminder could flash and create common knowledge for everyone, rather than that burden being on the moderator.","reply_to":"adamdangelo","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200527064837","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200527064837/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476559479046144","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1265476558749196288","date":"2020-05-27","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476558749196288","author":"adamdangelo","text":"More generally, if I were running Zoom, I would create a platform for anyone to write simple web app overlays to enable all kinds of these mediated interactions. A different app might let people in a large meeting vote +1 or -1 in real time to signal support for a choice.","reply_to":"adamdangelo","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200527171625","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200527171625/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476558749196288","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1265476558052970496","date":"2020-05-27","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476558052970496","author":"adamdangelo","text":"People could explicitly tell Zoom to move on when it was the end of their turn, or the moderator could override it. The person who is \"up next\" might get a special alert.","reply_to":"adamdangelo","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200527051027","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200527051027/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476558052970496","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1265476557289558017","date":"2020-05-27","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476557289558017","author":"adamdangelo","text":"Zoom should add a feature for a person running the meeting to organize this. It could let them choose an order for others and then guide the group through the process, with a number over each person's video to show the order, and highlighting to show whose turn it currently is.","reply_to":"adamdangelo","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200527071146","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200527071146/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476557289558017","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1265476556631076864","date":"2020-05-27","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476556631076864","author":"adamdangelo","text":"It's common in in-person meetings to \"go around the room\" and have everyone share their view on a topic. This is much harder over Zoom since everyone sees the group in a different order, and eye contact doesn't work. My thoughts:","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200527064253","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200527064253/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1265476556631076864","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1262989692007407618","date":"2020-05-20","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1262989692007407618","author":"adamdangelo","text":"@jonsid @sleepdiplomat Beware: https://t.co/VlcJYU9DJb","reply_to":"Jonsid","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200520063339","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200520063339/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1262989692007407618","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1252066045021450240","date":"2020-04-20","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1252066045021450240","author":"adamdangelo","text":"The most promising way out IMO is massive testing (like test everyone every week) but that is difficult to execute on and we are very very far from it and making slow progress.","reply_to":"adamdangelo","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200501115743","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200501115743/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1252066045021450240","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1252061736833699840","date":"2020-04-20","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1252061736833699840","author":"adamdangelo","text":"Vaccines will take more than a year. If we open up due to political pressure, cases will start to grow again which will then build support for another lockdown. Something big would need to change to have this be 4 months or less of the next 12.","reply_to":"adamdangelo","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200502035008","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200502035008/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1252061736833699840","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1252061242048434176","date":"2020-04-20","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1252061242048434176","author":"adamdangelo","text":"My bet is 5-12. R is around 1 so cases are barely declining. Singapore had to do a lockdown after executing on containment better than we can. Travel from other regions will bring in more cases. And the economic harm to a company like Google of employees WFH is not that bad.","reply_to":"adamdangelo","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200502021921","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200502021921/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1252061242048434176","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1251591882544574464","date":"2020-04-18","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1251591882544574464","author":"kevin","other_author":"kevin","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200418203138","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200418203138/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1251591882544574464","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1251577065310056450","date":"2020-04-18","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1251577065310056450","author":"adamdangelo","text":"Number of months out of the next 12 that Silicon Valley will be shut down (defined specifically as: majority of Google employees not working from the office)","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200418183200","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200418183200/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1251577065310056450","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1251576349006807041","date":"2020-04-18","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1251576349006807041","author":"adamdangelo","text":"@MarcBodnick Good idea. Will start over.","reply_to":"MarcBodnick","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200418192414","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200418192414/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1251576349006807041","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1245121340425695233","date":"2020-03-31","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1245121340425695233","author":"adamdangelo","text":"@andy_matuschak Also, we should expect the virus to keep spreading within families / roommates in the short term.","reply_to":"adamdangelo","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200331233057","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200331233057/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1245121340425695233","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1245119000272461825","date":"2020-03-31","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1245119000272461825","author":"adamdangelo","text":"@andy_matuschak I suspect R has decreased a ton but is still over 1 for certain sub-populations (e.g. employees of essential businesses).","reply_to":"andy_matuschak","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200331225754","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200331225754/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1245119000272461825","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1244996677053767681","date":"2020-03-31","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1244996677053767681","author":"adamdangelo","text":"Refers to a different Adam https://t.co/KMJwh4YmYy","reply_to":"adamdangelo","quoted":{"url":"https://x.com/paulkrugman/status/1244951311000506370","text":"Using annualized growth rates is deeply misleading here (not blaming Adam!) 34% annual rate is actually 8%. Still horrific, but not quite what you may think."},"live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200331155031","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200331155031/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1244996677053767681","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1241760322257432576","date":"2020-03-22","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1241760322257432576","author":"adamdangelo","text":"7) Quick correction to a typo in (4) above: when I said (Q2/Q2)^4 I meant (Q2/Q1)^4. Hope you all have a good Sunday.","reply_to":"adamdangelo","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200322171658","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200322171658/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1241760322257432576","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1241758983305572354","date":"2020-03-22","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1241758983305572354","author":"adamdangelo","text":"@GavinSBaker Hey I have seen this -24% number going around and I think it's not what GS meant; see https://t.co/dTVzLbI4dh","reply_to":"GavinSBaker","quoted":{"url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1241757534332960769","text":"1) A lot of people are trying to forecast the coronavirus impact on Q2 US GDP right now. I have one small piece to add to the conversation. There is a Goldman Sachs forecast from Friday that is being widely misreported as -24% from Q1 to Q2. The forecast is actually for -7%."},"live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200322181915","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200322181915/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1241758983305572354","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1241757543266951169","date":"2020-03-22","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1241757543266951169","author":"adamdangelo","text":"6) Obviously everything is changing so quickly and there is so much uncertainty that the error bars here are really wide. I would not be surprised if we do end up closer to -24%.","reply_to":"adamdangelo","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200322200207","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200322200207/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1241757543266951169","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1241757540909641729","date":"2020-03-22","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1241757540909641729","author":"adamdangelo","text":"5) So their number for Q2/Q1 is 1-(1-.24)^(1/4) = -7%.","reply_to":"adamdangelo","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200322170557","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200322170557/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1241757540909641729","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1241757539064111105","date":"2020-03-22","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1241757539064111105","author":"adamdangelo","text":"4) These are *annualized* rates, meaning the -24% number is (Q2/Q2)^4. This has to be the right interpretation because you wouldn't end up at -3.1% Q4/Q4 if you grow -6%, -24%, +12%, and then +10%.","reply_to":"adamdangelo","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200322172414","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200322172414/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1241757539064111105","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
{"id":"1241757536870469632","date":"2020-03-22","url":"https://x.com/adamdangelo/status/1241757536870469632","author":"adamdangelo","text":"3) The actual report says \"We now forecast quarter-on-quarter annualized growth rates of -6% in Q1, -24% in Q2, +12% in Q3, and +10% in Q4, leaving full-year growth at -3.8% on an annual average basis and -3.1% on a Q4/Q4 basis.\" https://t.co/OYhIhdSMNg","reply_to":"adamdangelo","live_status":200,"archived_at":"20200322163536","archive":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200322163536/https://twitter.com/adamdangelo/status/1241757536870469632","via":"wayback","read_at":"2026-09-30"}
